{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-horizon-conformal-invariance","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:horizon-conformal-invariance","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of horizon conformal invariance","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-horizon-conformal-invariance"],"text":"horizon-conformal-invariance-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:horizon-conformal-invariance\"></a><p><strong>Proof sketch.</strong>\nOn <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}</code>, the ideal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{h}</code> vanishes: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s|_{\\mathcal{H}} = 0</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s \\in A_0</code>. The quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_k/A_0</code> restricted to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}</code> depends solely on the equivalence class of sections modulo <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{h}</code>. Rescaling <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_0 \\mapsto \\lambda A_0</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda|_{\\mathcal{H}} \\neq 0</code> preserves the ideal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{h}</code>, because <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda s</code> vanishes on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}</code> if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s</code> does. The quotients are therefore identical on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/horizon-conformal-invariance-proof.md","heading":"Proof"}
